## 7. Battleground Blitz

The guide rates Affliction as **mid-tier** in Blitz because its damage is only average. It uses the same Soul Harvester build and PvP talents as arena.

- **Role:** spread damage in big team fights. Don't defend bases or take small skirmishes, since Affliction is weak 1v1.
- **Offense:** stay at max range, DoT the whole enemy team, then Haunt. Burst (Haunt, Unstable Affliction, Dark Harvest) the flag carrier or the kill target.
- **CC:** there's no Dampening in Blitz. Use Shadowfury and Howl of Terror on cooldown, and save Fear for emergencies. Damage matters more.
- **Utility:** Soulwell often. Place Demonic Gateway across height changes, such as across the river in Twin Peaks or from the lower to upper flag room.
- **Survival:** keep your Demonic Circle far back. Use Healthstone with Soulburn (3 charges).
- **Mobility:** too poor to carry the flag. Escort the carrier instead, and spam Curse of Exhaustion to peel.

| Map type | Plan |
|---|---|
| Capture the Flag (Warsong Gulch, Twin Peaks) | Join the opening team fight with your Circle set. Peel for your flag carrier through mid |
| Resource Race (Arathi Basin, Battle for Gilneas, Deepwind Gorge) | Never defend. Go with the team, keep your Circle in the back, and do damage |
| Eye of the Storm | Fight at the middle flag. Shadow Rift combos well with your team's knockbacks |
| Temple of Kotmogu | One map where you can carry an orb: Gateway upstairs, jump into the center, Circle out. Curse of Exhaustion with Jinx puts DoTs on chasers |

